  "output": {
    "answer": "Fair point — those four numbers really don't line up: crops as served came in at 78.2%, the same crops scored offline at 74.3%, a six-crop consensus proxy ranged 70.3% to 82.9%, and live lots pooled at 71.3%, dropping to 65.2% on lots that never auto-locked. I picked one bar on slide 12 and said explicitly which measure it was, rather than reporting a range, because you can't draw one trend line through four yardsticks that disagree — a single labeled number lets the audience know exactly what was measured, while a range would blur which of those four definitions it came from. The full spread is in the backup slide for anyone who wants it.",
